{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What does the nurse recognize as an example of Piaget\'s concrete operational thinking?',
opts:[
{t:'A 2-year-old child says, "It\'s nighttime" when his room is darkened.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The 7-year-old child\'s remark reflecting the cause and effect of germs and illness is an example of operational thinking. All other options are examples of preoperational thought, which is egocentric and symbolic.</i> The keyed answer is <b>A 7-year-old child says, "I am sick because I have germs in my chest."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'A 4-year-old child refers to the hospital as "my house."',c:false,r:'The 7-year-old child\'s remark reflecting the cause and effect of germs and illness is an example of operational thinking.'},
{t:'A 5-year-old child coloring a picture of a puppy says, "This is my puppy."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The 7-year-old child\'s remark reflecting the cause and effect of germs and illness is an example of operational thinking. All other options are examples of preoperational thought, which is egocentric and symbolic.</i> The keyed answer is <b>A 7-year-old child says, "I am sick because I have germs in my chest."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'A 7-year-old child says, "I am sick because I have germs in my chest."',c:true,r:'Correct. The 7-year-old child\'s remark reflecting the cause and effect of germs and illness is an example of operational thinking. All other options are examples of preoperational thought, which is egocentric and symbolic.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse has discussed with a mother the process of introducing solid foods to her 6-month-old infant. What statement by the mother leads the nurse to determine that learning has taken place?',
opts:[
