{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The mother of a 7-month-old infant states, "The baby is eating food now. Should I give him regular milk, too?" What is the nurse\'s best response?',
opts:[
{t:'"You should give the baby low-fat milk."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Whole milk should not be introduced before 1 year of age. Low-fat milk should not be introduced before 2 years of age.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Continue breast milk or iron-fortified formula until 1 year of age."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"Try the milk. See if he has any digestive problems."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Whole milk should not be introduced before 1 year of age. Low-fat milk should not be introduced before 2 years of age.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Continue breast milk or iron-fortified formula until 1 year of age."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"Continue breast milk or iron-fortified formula until 1 year of age."',c:true,r:'Correct. Whole milk should not be introduced before 1 year of age. Low-fat milk should not be introduced before 2 years of age.'},
{t:'"At this age, infants can tolerate lactose-free or soy-based milk."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Whole milk should not be introduced before 1 year of age. Low-fat milk should not be introduced before 2 years of age.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Continue breast milk or iron-fortified formula until 1 year of age."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

