{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse caring for a 4-year-old postoperative patient instructs him to blow bubbles. What nursing intervention is the nurse most likely implementing by using this form of therapeutic play?',
opts:[
{t:'Providing pain relief',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Play can also be therapeutic and aid in the recovery process. An example of therapeutic play is the game of having the child blow bubbles to promote deep breathing.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Encouraging deep breathing</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Encouraging deep breathing',c:true,r:'Correct. Play can also be therapeutic and aid in the recovery process. An example of therapeutic play is the game of having the child blow bubbles to promote deep breathing.'},
{t:'Decreasing risk of infection',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Play can also be therapeutic and aid in the recovery process. An example of therapeutic play is the game of having the child blow bubbles to promote deep breathing.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Encouraging deep breathing</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Maintaining body temperature',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Play can also be therapeutic and aid in the recovery process. An example of therapeutic play is the game of having the child blow bubbles to promote deep breathing.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Encouraging deep breathing</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The mother of a 7-year-old pediatric patient asks the nurse about her child\'s sleep requirement. What is the most accurate response by the nurse?',
opts:[
{t:'"7 to 10 hours a night"',c:false,r:'The neonate sleeps 8 to 9 hours per night and naps an equal amount of time during the day.'},
{t:'"5 to 7 hours a night with one daytime nap"',c:false,r:'The 2-year-old child may sleep 10 hours during the night and have only one short daytime nap.'},
{t:'"11 to 13 hours a night"',c:true,r:'Correct. Sleep patterns vary with age. The neonate sleeps 8 to 9 hours per night and naps an equal amount of time during the day. The 2-year-old child may sleep 10 hours during the night and have only one short daytime nap. The 7-year-old child usually requires 11 to 13 hours of sleep and rarely has a daytime nap. These patterns may be altered by cultural practices.'},
{t:'"4 to 6 hours a night with two daytime naps"',c:false,r:'The neonate sleeps 8 to 9 hours per night and naps an equal amount of time during the day.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'How do children differ from adults? (Select all that apply.)',
opts:[
{t:'Higher metabolic rate',c:true,r:'Correct. Children are in a continuous growth and development pattern. Children have a greater surface area and a higher metabolic rate. All of their organ systems are not mature.'},
{t:'Greater surface area in relation to their weight',c:true,r:'Correct. Children are in a continuous growth and development pattern. Children have a greater surface area and a higher metabolic rate. All of their organ systems are not mature.'},
{t:'Less mature organ systems',c:true,r:'Correct. Children are in a continuous growth and development pattern. Children have a greater surface area and a higher metabolic rate. All of their organ systems are not mature.'},
{t:'More fluid reserves',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Children are in a continuous growth and development pattern. Children have a greater surface area and a higher metabolic rate. All of their organ systems are not mature.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Higher metabolic rate / Greater surface area in relation to their weight / Less mature organ systems / Continuously changing growth and development pattern</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Continuously changing growth and development pattern',c:true,r:'Correct. Children are in a continuous growth and development pattern. Children have a greater surface area and a higher metabolic rate. All of their organ systems are not mature.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 15',topic:'Growth, development, nutrition',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'What approaches should the nurse suggest for introducing a toddler to new foods? (Select all that apply.)',
opts:[
