{t:'Avoid showing personal likes or dislikes.',c:true,r:'Correct. Foods should be introduced in small, warm servings, one food at a time. Sweets and milk should not be offered until after solid food.'},
{t:'Offer foods in small amounts, less than a teaspoon.',c:true,r:'Correct. Foods should be introduced in small, warm servings, one food at a time. Sweets and milk should not be offered until after solid food.'},
{t:'Entice the toddler to eat with sweets.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Foods should be introduced in small, warm servings, one food at a time. Sweets and milk should not be offered until after solid food.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Serve one food at a time. / Avoid showing personal likes or dislikes. / Offer foods in small amounts, less than a teaspoon. / Serve food warm.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Serve food warm.',c:true,r:'Correct. Foods should be introduced in small, warm servings, one food at a time. Sweets and milk should not be offered until after solid food.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

