{t:'Art play should be used sparingly.',c:false,r:'The bank does not argue this one down directly. The keyed answer is <b>Understanding of child–parent relationships can be gained by observing play. / Play encourages self-expression. / Play provides a sense of accomplishment.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option. If you cannot say it, that is the gap.'},
{t:'Use of computer/video games is detrimental.',c:false,r:'The bank does not argue this one down directly. The keyed answer is <b>Understanding of child–parent relationships can be gained by observing play. / Play encourages self-expression. / Play provides a sense of accomplishment.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option. If you cannot say it, that is the gap.'},
{t:'Understanding of child–parent relationships can be gained by observing play.',c:true,r:'Correct. Art is an appropriate play activity at almost any age and provides an avenue for experimentation as well as for creative expression and a feeling of accomplishment in the child. Observing the child at play can aid in assessing growth and development and understanding the child\'s relationships with family members. Any plan of care for a hospitalized child of any age should include a play activity that either encourages growth and development or encourages the expression of thoughts and feelings. Computer programs are popular with all age groups, providing problem-solving skills, manipulative skills, and opportunities for new learning.'},
{t:'Play encourages self-expression.',c:true,r:'Correct. Art is an appropriate play activity at almost any age and provides an avenue for experimentation as well as for creative expression and a feeling of accomplishment in the child. Observing the child at play can aid in assessing growth and development and understanding the child\'s relationships with family members. Any plan of care for a hospitalized child of any age should include a play activity that either encourages growth and development or encourages the expression of thoughts and feelings. Computer programs are popular with all age groups, providing problem-solving skills, manipulative skills, and opportunities for new learning.'},
{t:'Play provides a sense of accomplishment.',c:true,r:'Correct. Art is an appropriate play activity at almost any age and provides an avenue for experimentation as well as for creative expression and a feeling of accomplishment in the child. Observing the child at play can aid in assessing growth and development and understanding the child\'s relationships with family members. Any plan of care for a hospitalized child of any age should include a play activity that either encourages growth and development or encourages the expression of thoughts and feelings. Computer programs are popular with all age groups, providing problem-solving skills, manipulative skills, and opportunities for new learning.'}],
teach:'<b>An Overview of Growth, Development, and Nutrition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 15 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

