{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'A 2-year-old child has been crying constantly for his mother since he was hospitalized 3 days ago. What does this behavior suggest?',
opts:[
{t:'The toddler feels abandoned by his mother.',c:true,r:'Correct. Unless toddlers are extremely ill, their grief and sense of abandonment during hospitalization are obvious.'},
{t:'The child still has not adjusted to his hospitalization.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Unless toddlers are extremely ill, their grief and sense of abandonment during hospitalization are obvious.</i> The keyed answer is <b>The toddler feels abandoned by his mother.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'The child is not separated from his mother often.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Unless toddlers are extremely ill, their grief and sense of abandonment during hospitalization are obvious.</i> The keyed answer is <b>The toddler feels abandoned by his mother.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'There is a poor mother–child bond.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Unless toddlers are extremely ill, their grief and sense of abandonment during hospitalization are obvious.</i> The keyed answer is <b>The toddler feels abandoned by his mother.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

