{t:'Providing a way for the child to express his feelings',c:true,r:'Correct. After treatments, the nurse should encourage children to draw and talk about their drawings or to act out their feelings through puppet play.'},
{t:'Encouraging quiet play',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>After treatments, the nurse should encourage children to draw and talk about their drawings or to act out their feelings through puppet play.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Providing a way for the child to express his feelings</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Distracting the child from thinking about the pain',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>After treatments, the nurse should encourage children to draw and talk about their drawings or to act out their feelings through puppet play.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Providing a way for the child to express his feelings</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What is the best suggestion by the nurse when parents ask, "When is the best time to begin to prepare a 5-year-old child for surgery and hospitalization?"',
