{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse notices that the mother of a child with cerebral palsy corrects and redoes many of the things the nurse does for her child. What is the nurse\'s most appropriate response to this mother?',
opts:[
{t:'"Would you like to do all of your child\'s care?"',c:false,r:'The person who cares daily for the child with a chronic illness can provide information that will best guarantee continuity of care between the home and the hospital.'},
{t:'"I\'m doing the very best job that I can with your child."',c:false,r:'The person who cares daily for the child with a chronic illness can provide information that will best guarantee continuity of care between the home and the hospital.'},
{t:'"Why don\'t you go have a cup of coffee? You are going to be exhausted if you don\'t take a break."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The person who cares daily for the child with a chronic illness can provide information that will best guarantee continuity of care between the home and the hospital.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"I\'d love for you to share with me some of the special things you do for your child."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"I\'d love for you to share with me some of the special things you do for your child."',c:true,r:'Correct. The person who cares daily for the child with a chronic illness can provide information that will best guarantee continuity of care between the home and the hospital.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The mother of a hospitalized toddler states, "He cries when I visit. Maybe I should just stay away." What is the nurse\'s best response?',
opts:[
{t:'"Perhaps you are right. He only gets upset when you have to leave."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>During the second stage of separation anxiety (despair), the child is quiet, is not crying, and is sad and depressed. The child will revert to protest when the parent arrives for a visit.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"It is important that you are here. This is a common reaction in children when they are separated from their parents."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"It is important that you are here. This is a common reaction in children when they are separated from their parents."',c:true,r:'Correct. During the second stage of separation anxiety (despair), the child is quiet, is not crying, and is sad and depressed. The child will revert to protest when the parent arrives for a visit.'},
{t:'"It might be easier for your child if you would stay with him, but this decision is up to you."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>During the second stage of separation anxiety (despair), the child is quiet, is not crying, and is sad and depressed. The child will revert to protest when the parent arrives for a visit.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"It is important that you are here. This is a common reaction in children when they are separated from their parents."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"We take good care of him and he seems fine when you are not here."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>During the second stage of separation anxiety (despair), the child is quiet, is not crying, and is sad and depressed. The child will revert to protest when the parent arrives for a visit.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"It is important that you are here. This is a common reaction in children when they are separated from their parents."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

