{t:'"Addiction is rare in children when opiates are given for pain."',c:true,r:'Correct. Addiction is rare in children.'},
{t:'"Addictive behaviors are easy to assess. The drug will be stopped if that happens."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Addiction is rare in children.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Addiction is rare in children when opiates are given for pain."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Intervention'},

{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
