{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'What will the nurse include when documenting the discharge of a pediatric patient? (Select all that apply.)',
opts:[
{t:'Time of discharge',c:true,r:'Correct. Information that should be included in the discharge note include time of discharge, adults accompanying the child and relationship to the child, condition of the child, and method of transportation. It should also be documented that instructions were given to parents.'},
{t:'Adult(s) accompanying the child and the relationship to the child',c:true,r:'Correct. Information that should be included in the discharge note include time of discharge, adults accompanying the child and relationship to the child, condition of the child, and method of transportation. It should also be documented that instructions were given to parents.'},
{t:'Condition of the child',c:true,r:'Correct. Information that should be included in the discharge note include time of discharge, adults accompanying the child and relationship to the child, condition of the child, and method of transportation. It should also be documented that instructions were given to parents.'},
{t:'Method of transportation',c:true,r:'Correct. Information that should be included in the discharge note include time of discharge, adults accompanying the child and relationship to the child, condition of the child, and method of transportation. It should also be documented that instructions were given to parents.'},
{t:'Instructions that were given to physician',c:false,r:'It should also be documented that instructions were given to parents.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child\'s Experience of Hospitalization</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 21 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 21',topic:'Hospitalized child',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
