{t:'4 seconds',c:false,r:'Capillary refill in 3 seconds or less is determined to be indicative of adequate perfusion.'},
{t:'5 seconds',c:false,r:'Capillary refill in 3 seconds or less is determined to be indicative of adequate perfusion.'},
{t:'6 seconds',c:false,r:'Capillary refill in 3 seconds or less is determined to be indicative of adequate perfusion.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The parent of a child with osteomyelitis asks why his child is in so much pain. What will the nurse respond causes the pain experienced with osteomyelitis?',
opts:[
{t:'"Pressure of inelastic bone"',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Osteomyelitis is an infection of the bone. Inflammation produces an exudate that collects under the marrow and cortex of the bone. The vessels are compressed and thrombosis occurs, producing ischemia and pain.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Purulent drainage in the bone marrow"</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"Purulent drainage in the bone marrow"',c:true,r:'Correct. Osteomyelitis is an infection of the bone. Inflammation produces an exudate that collects under the marrow and cortex of the bone. The vessels are compressed and thrombosis occurs, producing ischemia and pain.'},
{t:'"The cast applied on the extremity"',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Osteomyelitis is an infection of the bone. Inflammation produces an exudate that collects under the marrow and cortex of the bone. The vessels are compressed and thrombosis occurs, producing ischemia and pain.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Purulent drainage in the bone marrow"</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"Circulatory congestion of the skin"',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Osteomyelitis is an infection of the bone. Inflammation produces an exudate that collects under the marrow and cortex of the bone. The vessels are compressed and thrombosis occurs, producing ischemia and pain.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Purulent drainage in the bone marrow"</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'A child hospitalized for treatment of osteomyelitis complains that he is tired of being sick and wants to know when the antibiotic protocol will end. How long will the nurse indicate that antibiotic therapy will probably last?',
opts:[
{t:'2 weeks',c:false,r:'Because osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone, antibiotics are given intravenously for 4 to 6 weeks.'},
{t:'6 weeks',c:true,r:'Correct. Because osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone, antibiotics are given intravenously for 4 to 6 weeks.'},
{t:'2 months',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Because osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone, antibiotics are given intravenously for 4 to 6 weeks.</i> The keyed answer is <b>6 weeks</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'3 months',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Because osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone, antibiotics are given intravenously for 4 to 6 weeks.</i> The keyed answer is <b>6 weeks</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

