{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'A 13-year-old girl is diagnosed with functional scoliosis. What does the nurse explain as the cause of this spinal curvature defect?',
opts:[
{t:'Juvenile rheumatoid arthritis',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Functional scoliosis usually is caused by poor posture, and it is not a spinal disease.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Poor posture</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
