{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What intervention is appropriate for a nurse assessing a preadolescent child for scoliosis?',
opts:[
{t:'Ask the child to bend forward at the waist and observe the child\'s back for asymmetry.',c:true,r:'Correct. The nurse looks at the back as the child bends forward for general body alignment and asymmetry.'},
{t:'Observe the gait while the child is walking forward heel to toe.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse looks at the back as the child bends forward for general body alignment and asymmetry.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Ask the child to bend forward at the waist and observe the child\'s back for asymmetry.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Have the child flex the knees and look for uneven knee height.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse looks at the back as the child bends forward for general body alignment and asymmetry.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Ask the child to bend forward at the waist and observe the child\'s back for asymmetry.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Look at the child\'s shoulders and hips while fully clothed.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse looks at the back as the child bends forward for general body alignment and asymmetry.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Ask the child to bend forward at the waist and observe the child\'s back for asymmetry.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
