{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What nursing action will significantly decrease the risk of serious complications for a child in Bryant\'s traction?',
opts:[
{t:'Neurovascular checks are done frequently.',c:true,r:'Correct. The nurse caring for a child in traction must be alert for Volkmann\'s ischemia, which occurs when circulation is obstructed.'},
{t:'Bandages are wrapped tightly.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse caring for a child in traction must be alert for Volkmann\'s ischemia, which occurs when circulation is obstructed.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Neurovascular checks are done frequently.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'The child is restrained from rolling over.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse caring for a child in traction must be alert for Volkmann\'s ischemia, which occurs when circulation is obstructed.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Neurovascular checks are done frequently.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'The child\'s buttocks are resting on the bed.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The nurse caring for a child in traction must be alert for Volkmann\'s ischemia, which occurs when circulation is obstructed.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Neurovascular checks are done frequently.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

