{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'A pediatric nurse is assisting with the care of a child diagnosed with a fractured femur. What type of fracture would be the most likely to alert the nurse to the possibility of physical abuse?',
opts:[
{t:'Stress fracture',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>A spiral fracture of the femur is caused by a forceful twisting motion. When the history of an injury does not correlate with x-ray findings, child abuse should be suspected because spiral fractures can be the result of manual twisting of the extremity.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Spiral fracture</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Compound fracture',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>A spiral fracture of the femur is caused by a forceful twisting motion. When the history of an injury does not correlate with x-ray findings, child abuse should be suspected because spiral fractures can be the result of manual twisting of the extremity.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Spiral fracture</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Spiral fracture',c:true,r:'Correct. A spiral fracture of the femur is caused by a forceful twisting motion. When the history of an injury does not correlate with x-ray findings, child abuse should be suspected because spiral fractures can be the result of manual twisting of the extremity.'},
{t:'Greenstick fracture',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>A spiral fracture of the femur is caused by a forceful twisting motion. When the history of an injury does not correlate with x-ray findings, child abuse should be suspected because spiral fractures can be the result of manual twisting of the extremity.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Spiral fracture</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

