{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse demonstrates which similarities among all traction devices? (Select all that apply.)',
opts:[
{t:'Pull the limb into extension.',c:true,r:'Correct. Tractions are designed to immobilize and pull limbs into extension. Traction can also align broken bones and decrease muscle spasm. Although some traction devices may relieve pain, many may actually cause pain.'},
{t:'Decrease muscle spasm.',c:true,r:'Correct. Tractions are designed to immobilize and pull limbs into extension. Traction can also align broken bones and decrease muscle spasm. Although some traction devices may relieve pain, many may actually cause pain.'},
{t:'Reduce pain.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Tractions are designed to immobilize and pull limbs into extension. Traction can also align broken bones and decrease muscle spasm. Although some traction devices may relieve pain, many may actually cause pain.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Pull the limb into extension. / Decrease muscle spasm. / Align two bone fragments. / Immobilize the limb.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Align two bone fragments.',c:true,r:'Correct. Tractions are designed to immobilize and pull limbs into extension. Traction can also align broken bones and decrease muscle spasm. Although some traction devices may relieve pain, many may actually cause pain.'},
{t:'Immobilize the limb.',c:true,r:'Correct. Tractions are designed to immobilize and pull limbs into extension. Traction can also align broken bones and decrease muscle spasm. Although some traction devices may relieve pain, many may actually cause pain.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse performing a neurovascular check on a limb in traction would report and document which finding(s) as indicative of altered circulation? (Select all that apply.)',
