{ch:'Ch 24',topic:'Musculoskeletal (peds)',bank:true,type:'SATA',vuln:'low',
stem:'How does the pediatric skeletal system differ from that of the adult? (Select all that apply.)',
opts:[
{t:'Lower mineral content',c:true,r:'Correct. The child\'s skeletal system has lower mineral content, greater porosity, open epiphyses, greater bone strength, and a thicker periosteum.'},
{t:'More ossification',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The child\'s skeletal system has lower mineral content, greater porosity, open epiphyses, greater bone strength, and a thicker periosteum.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Lower mineral content / Open epiphyses / Greater strength</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Open epiphyses',c:true,r:'Correct. The child\'s skeletal system has lower mineral content, greater porosity, open epiphyses, greater bone strength, and a thicker periosteum.'},
{t:'Less porosity',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The child\'s skeletal system has lower mineral content, greater porosity, open epiphyses, greater bone strength, and a thicker periosteum.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Lower mineral content / Open epiphyses / Greater strength</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Greater strength',c:true,r:'Correct. The child\'s skeletal system has lower mineral content, greater porosity, open epiphyses, greater bone strength, and a thicker periosteum.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Musculoskeletal Condition</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 24 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: N/A'},

