{t:'Oxygen saturation of 90%',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>A "quiet chest" after assessment of wheezing indicates occlusion of air pathways and impending respiratory arrest. All other options are within normal range for infants undergoing oxygen administration.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"Quiet chest" from previous assessment of wheezing</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
