{t:'Expiratory wheezing',c:true,r:'Correct. The child experiencing an acute asthma attack wheezes as air moves in and out of the narrowed airways. The expiratory wheeze is most pronounced.'},
{t:'Decreased breath sounds at lung bases',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The child experiencing an acute asthma attack wheezes as air moves in and out of the narrowed airways. The expiratory wheeze is most pronounced.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Expiratory wheezing</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
