{t:'Place the child in a humidified cool mist tent with oxygen.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>This position is comfortable and allows maximum use of the accessory muscles for breathing. Sedatives would mask symptoms of increasing air hunger. Carbonated beverages are contraindicated in persons with dyspnea.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Position the child with arms resting on the overbed table.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Administer sedatives as ordered to decrease anxiety.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>This position is comfortable and allows maximum use of the accessory muscles for breathing. Sedatives would mask symptoms of increasing air hunger. Carbonated beverages are contraindicated in persons with dyspnea.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Position the child with arms resting on the overbed table.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Position the child with arms resting on the overbed table.',c:true,r:'Correct. This position is comfortable and allows maximum use of the accessory muscles for breathing. Sedatives would mask symptoms of increasing air hunger. Carbonated beverages are contraindicated in persons with dyspnea.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 25',topic:'Respiratory (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What should the nurse explain to the parent of a child with exercise-induced asthma about when to inhale Cromolyn?',
opts:[
{t:'Before exercise to prevent attacks',c:true,r:'Correct. Anti-inflammatory inhalants are taken before exercise to prevent attacks. These drugs can do nothing for the attack in progress. They are meant to be used as prophylactic therapies.'},
{t:'At the initial onset of the attack',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Anti-inflammatory inhalants are taken before exercise to prevent attacks. These drugs can do nothing for the attack in progress. They are meant to be used as prophylactic therapies.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Before exercise to prevent attacks</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'During the attack to relieve symptoms',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Anti-inflammatory inhalants are taken before exercise to prevent attacks. These drugs can do nothing for the attack in progress. They are meant to be used as prophylactic therapies.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Before exercise to prevent attacks</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'As often as 4 times a day',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Anti-inflammatory inhalants are taken before exercise to prevent attacks. These drugs can do nothing for the attack in progress. They are meant to be used as prophylactic therapies.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Before exercise to prevent attacks</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 25',topic:'Respiratory (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The parents of a 3-month-old infant with cystic fibrosis (CF) want to know how their child got this disease, because no one in either of their families has CF. What is the nurse\'s best response based on the understanding of CF?',
opts:[
{t:'Only one parent carries the CF gene.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Cystic fibrosis is an inherited disease. Both parents must be carriers of the CF gene for the child to have the disease.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Both parents are carriers of the CF gene.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Both parents are carriers of the CF gene.',c:true,r:'Correct. Cystic fibrosis is an inherited disease. Both parents must be carriers of the CF gene for the child to have the disease.'},
{t:'The inheritance pattern is multifactorial.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Cystic fibrosis is an inherited disease. Both parents must be carriers of the CF gene for the child to have the disease.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Both parents are carriers of the CF gene.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'The result is probably a genetic mutation.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Cystic fibrosis is an inherited disease. Both parents must be carriers of the CF gene for the child to have the disease.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Both parents are carriers of the CF gene.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 25',topic:'Respiratory (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'Which statement indicates that the child\'s parents understand how to perform respiratory therapy?',
opts:[
