{t:'"We give her respiratory treatments when she is coughing a lot."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Postural drainage for the child with CF is done following nebulization. Therapy is best scheduled before meals or at least 1 hour after eating to prevent vomiting.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"We give the aerosol followed by postural drainage before meals."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"We give the aerosol followed by postural drainage before meals."',c:true,r:'Correct. Postural drainage for the child with CF is done following nebulization. Therapy is best scheduled before meals or at least 1 hour after eating to prevent vomiting.'},
{t:'"She needs respiratory therapy every day when she has an infection."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Postural drainage for the child with CF is done following nebulization. Therapy is best scheduled before meals or at least 1 hour after eating to prevent vomiting.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"We give the aerosol followed by postural drainage before meals."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Evaluation'},

{ch:'Ch 25',topic:'Respiratory (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What will the nurse teach the child with cystic fibrosis to take in order to facilitate digestion and absorption of nutrients?',
opts:[
{t:'Pancreatic enzymes',c:true,r:'Correct. An oral pancreatic enzyme is given to the child with every meal and with snacks to replace the pancreatic enzymes that the child\'s body cannot produce.'},
