{t:'Fat-soluble vitamins',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>An oral pancreatic enzyme is given to the child with every meal and with snacks to replace the pancreatic enzymes that the child\'s body cannot produce.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Pancreatic enzymes</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Salt supplements',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>An oral pancreatic enzyme is given to the child with every meal and with snacks to replace the pancreatic enzymes that the child\'s body cannot produce.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Pancreatic enzymes</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

