{ch:'Ch 25',topic:'Respiratory (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The nurse offers a variety of fluids to a 5-year-old asthmatic child to compensate for the fluid loss through dyspnea. Which fluids are most appropriate?',
opts:[
{t:'Room temperature water',c:true,r:'Correct. Room temperature fluids are the best. Carbonated and iced beverages increase spasm. Milk stimulates mucus production.'},
{t:'Carbonated beverages',c:false,r:'Carbonated and iced beverages increase spasm.'},
{t:'Iced fruit juice',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Room temperature fluids are the best. Carbonated and iced beverages increase spasm. Milk stimulates mucus production.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Room temperature water</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Cold milk',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Room temperature fluids are the best. Carbonated and iced beverages increase spasm. Milk stimulates mucus production.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Room temperature water</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Respiratory Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 25 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

