{t:'Sitting the infant up in an infant seat',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>The American Academy of Pediatrics recommends that all healthy infants be placed in the supine or side-lying position on a firm mattress to prevent SIDS.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Placing infants on their backs or sides for sleep</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
