{t:'Hypoxia',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>As the effects of rheumatic fever affect the central nervous system, the child may develop Sydenham\'s chorea, manifested by involuntary, purposeless movements of the limbs.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Sydenham\'s chorea</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'Sydenham\'s chorea',c:true,r:'Correct. As the effects of rheumatic fever affect the central nervous system, the child may develop Sydenham\'s chorea, manifested by involuntary, purposeless movements of the limbs.'},
{t:'Decreasing level of consciousness',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>As the effects of rheumatic fever affect the central nervous system, the child may develop Sydenham\'s chorea, manifested by involuntary, purposeless movements of the limbs.</i> The keyed answer is <b>Sydenham\'s chorea</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Cardiovascular Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 26 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Data Collection'},

{ch:'Ch 26',topic:'Cardiovascular (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
