opts:[
{t:'1 year',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>Children who recover from rheumatic fever should have a chemoprophylaxis protocol of penicillin G injections (about 200,000 units per dose) for a minimum of 5 years or up to the age of 18 years to prevent further bouts of rheumatic fever.</i> The keyed answer is <b>5 years</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'2 years',c:false,r:'Children who recover from rheumatic fever should have a chemoprophylaxis protocol of penicillin G injections (about 200,000 units per dose) for a minimum of 5 years or up to the age of 18 years to prevent further bouts of rheumatic fever.'},
{t:'5 years',c:true,r:'Correct. Children who recover from rheumatic fever should have a chemoprophylaxis protocol of penicillin G injections (about 200,000 units per dose) for a minimum of 5 years or up to the age of 18 years to prevent further bouts of rheumatic fever.'},
{t:'10 years',c:false,r:'Children who recover from rheumatic fever should have a chemoprophylaxis protocol of penicillin G injections (about 200,000 units per dose) for a minimum of 5 years or up to the age of 18 years to prevent further bouts of rheumatic fever.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Cardiovascular Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 26 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

{ch:'Ch 26',topic:'Cardiovascular (peds)',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'What is accurate about the characteristics of high-density lipoproteins (HDLs)?',
opts:[
{t:'They have high amounts of triglycerides.',c:false,r:'HDLs have low amounts of triglycerides, large amounts of proteins, and low amount of cholesterol, and are excreted via the liver.'},
{t:'They have only small amounts of protein.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>HDLs have low amounts of triglycerides, large amounts of proteins, and low amount of cholesterol, and are excreted via the liver. They have no role in the production of steroids.</i> The keyed answer is <b>They have little cholesterol.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'They have little cholesterol.',c:true,r:'Correct. HDLs have low amounts of triglycerides, large amounts of proteins, and low amount of cholesterol, and are excreted via the liver. They have no role in the production of steroids.'},
{t:'They aid in steroid production.',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>HDLs have low amounts of triglycerides, large amounts of proteins, and low amount of cholesterol, and are excreted via the liver. They have no role in the production of steroids.</i> The keyed answer is <b>They have little cholesterol.</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>The Child with a Cardiovascular Disorder</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 26 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Planning'},

