{ch:'Ch 34',topic:'Complementary therapies',bank:true,type:'MC',vuln:'low',
stem:'The pregnant patient with a stasis ulcer asks if she might be a candidate for hyperbaric oxygen therapy (HBOT). What is the nurse\'s best response?',
opts:[
{t:'"Yes. Hyperbaric oxygen therapy should have no harmful effect on your baby."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>High concentrations of oxygen in the mother\'s blood can cause closure of the ductus arteriosus and cause fetal death.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"No. High amounts of oxygen in your system will cause changes in your baby\'s heart."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"No. High amounts of oxygen in your system will cause changes in your baby\'s heart."',c:true,r:'Correct. High concentrations of oxygen in the mother\'s blood can cause closure of the ductus arteriosus and cause fetal death.'},
{t:'"Yes. Hyperbaric oxygen therapy is a much better option than using antibiotics."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>High concentrations of oxygen in the mother\'s blood can cause closure of the ductus arteriosus and cause fetal death.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"No. High amounts of oxygen in your system will cause changes in your baby\'s heart."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'},
{t:'"No. Hyperbaric oxygen therapy may cause the placenta to separate from the uterine wall."',c:false,r:'Not the keyed answer. What the bank says about this item: <i>High concentrations of oxygen in the mother\'s blood can cause closure of the ductus arteriosus and cause fetal death.</i> The keyed answer is <b>"No. High amounts of oxygen in your system will cause changes in your baby\'s heart."</b> &mdash; say out loud why that beats this option.'}],
teach:'<b>Complementary and Alternative Therapies in Maternity and Pediatric Nursing</b> &middot; Leifer 10e test bank, Ch 34 item. Cognitive level: Cognitive. Bank tags: Nursing Process Step: Implementation'},

